{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And Elohim went up from Abraham.</b> Rashi explained: from here we learn that the patriarchs are themselves the divine Chariot. This teaches that there is no intermediary between HaShem, blessed be He, and the patriarchs, and their partition is within, before the partition of the ministering angels — as Rashi explained on the verse ״כָּעֵת יֵאָמֵר לְיַעֲקֹב״ and so forth (Numbers 23:23), and as it is written (Deuteronomy 33:27) ״מְעֹנָה אֱלֹהֵי קֶדֶם וּמִתַּחַת זְרֹעֹת עוֹלָם״. For the Holy One, blessed be He, is His dwelling above, and beneath Him are the patriarchs, who are זְרֹעֹת עוֹלָם (the everlasting arms), for they uphold the Throne, as it were; and as it is written (Deuteronomy 33:26) ״רֹכֵב שָׁמַיִם בְּעֶזְרֶךָ״ — that is to say, 'You help Me,' as it were, in the manner that they said (Yalkut Shimoni on Psalms, remez 879) that the righteous add strength to the power above, and so forth. And the reason why it says ״וַיַּעַל אֱלֹהִים״ is that Abraham should occupy himself with the circumcision and not delay while the Shechinah is with him."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:28:30.978329340Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}